+**Analysis code and provenance.** The analysis follows four rules. (i) Every reported number is traced to an output file, a stated derivation or a cited source, and listed in a numbers manifest with the file's SHA-256 where it has one; the manifest will be released with the code. (ii) A prediction counts as registered only if it was committed to version control before the first output it predicts; otherwise a timestamped prediction is *pre-specified* (exploratory), and analyses written after a first output are post hoc (times: Supplementary S4). (iii) Model-produced signals are never treated as gold or as human evidence; one set of new human labels was collected, for the object gold of XM3600-600, under a labelling plan and an analysis registration fixed before anyone but the annotator opened a label value (Section 6.7). (iv) Every cited identifier was checked on a primary record. The re-scoring code reproduced four published CHAIR rows to within 0.6 points on every reported column (Supplementary S3), and the XM3600 evaluator verified the registered hashes of its frozen inputs (Supplementary Table S4.0, row X-0). The code, matchers, registration files, manifest and score-only result files will be deposited, before review, as a restricted record that reviewers will be able to open through the editor (Data availability); the record is not public during review, and the code has not yet been run outside the authors' group.
 
